 "notes": [
  [
   "Power: the switch common is the 3.3 V rail (XIAO 3V3 pin and the LEDs). Position 1 = badge 3.3 V feeds the rail. Position 2 (OFF) ties D1 to the rail; position 3 (USB) leaves the badge disconnected.",
   [
    38.1,
    96.52
   ]
  ],
  [
   "On USB-BAT the XIAO powers the rail itself, from USB-C or the LiPo on J2 (charged by the XIAO). In OFF the firmware sees D1 high and blanks the LEDs (a sleep, not a hard cut, with a LiPo attached). No coin cell.",
   [
    38.1,
    100.33
   ]
  ],
  [
   "Do not plug in USB with the switch on SAO while on a badge: two 3.3 V regulators would share one rail.",
   [
    38.1,
    104.14
   ]
  ],
  [
   "D1..D4 = SK6805 side-firing RGB round the bottom of the helmet, chained D1 (right, seen from the front) to D4 (left), as on the original. C1 = 100 nF at the LEDs' supply.",
   [
    38.1,
    107.94999999999999
   ]
  ],
  [
   "R2, R3: 330 ohm on the SAO GPIO pins per docs/standard.md. R1: 330 ohm on the LED data line. R4: 330 ohm in the OFF sense line (harmless; it lets the badge 3.3 V track cross it). R2, R3 and R4 each let one other track pass between their pads: the board is routed on the back copper only.",
   [
    38.1,
    111.75999999999999
   ]
  ],
  [
   "The maker's two 10 k I2C pull-ups were dropped (the badge provides them; docs/standard.md section 1). Mode button = the XIAO's own BOOT button.",
   [
    38.1,
    115.57
   ]
  ]
 ]
}